  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Public Matrix*Vector and Vector*Matrix now use a lazy storage-neutral dispatcher. ZZ and QQ cross one generated FLINT-resource boundary, GF(2) borrows M4RI in compiled typed Python, and other packed prime fields use compiler-owned residue buffers. Sage coercion, zero shapes, skew exact values, fresh mutable results, and dimension errors are covered by focused regression tests.",
    "risks": [
      "Extension and approximate fields deliberately retain the former temporary row/column matrix fallback until they acquire declared vector ABIs.",
      "The generated FFI wrappers increase the native-integration package ratchet from 605000 to 612000 bytes.",
      "At 500x500, the lazy public dispatcher currently adds enough fixed overhead that ZZ and QQ trail the reconstructed temporary-matrix path; packed prime products remain about twice as fast."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Run portable and non-x64 validation after integration.",
      "Measure whether lazy Python orchestration overhead merits a fused public dispatch helper for very small exact products."
    ]
  }
